smash to the other side of the court is called a &#8220;<strong>cross court smash<\/strong>&#8220;.<\/p>\n<p>The <strong>technique<\/strong> to hit a cross court smash is exactly the same as performing the normal smash.<\/p>\n<h3>Take the shuttle at the Highest Point Possible<\/h3>\n<p>You won&#8217;t be able get a steep angle with a cross court smash.<\/p>\n<p>To see why is this case, we&#8217;ll compare the cross court smash against the forward smash.<\/p>\n<h4>The Forward Smash<\/h4>\n<p class=\"Thumbnail\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"aligncenter wp-image-3280 \" src=\"http:\/\/masterbadminton.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2016\/05\/Overhead-Smash-v3.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"601\" height=\"427\" srcset=\"https:\/\/masterbadminton.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2016\/05\/Overhead-Smash-v3.png 1500w, https:\/\/masterbadminton.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2016\/05\/Overhead-Smash-v3-300x213.png 300w, https:\/\/masterbadminton.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2016\/05\/Overhead-Smash-v3-1024x728.png 1024w, https:\/\/masterbadminton.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2016\/05\/Overhead-Smash-v3-768x546.png 768w, https:\/\/masterbadminton.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2016\/05\/Overhead-Smash-v3-18x12.png 18w, https:\/\/masterbadminton.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2016\/05\/Overhead-Smash-v3-640x455.png 640w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 601px) 100vw, 601px\" \/><\/p>\n<p>When you hit the <strong>forward smash<\/strong>, the shuttlecock travels a <strong>shorter distance<\/strong> before it reaches the ground.<\/p>\n<p>In other words, the shuttlecock will travel a shorter distance to reach the net. In order to get a steep angle, smash while the shuttle is still high.<\/p>\n<h4>The Cross Court Smash<\/h4>\n<p>The <strong>cross court smash<\/strong> requires a <strong>longer distance<\/strong> before the shuttlecock reaches the ground.<\/p>\n<p>In other words, the shuttlecock will travel a longer distance to reach the net.<\/p>\n<p>So, to get a good angle for your cross court smash, take the shuttle from the highest point possible!<\/p>\n<p>Otherwise, your shot will not pass the net. If your shot is too flat, your cross court smash will go wide.<\/p>\n<p>Think twice if you want to hit a full cross court smash from your baseline (or anywhere too far back of your court). The angle will be VERY tight!<\/p>\n<h3>Jumping Smash as a Solution<\/h3>\n<p>If you can perform the <a href=\"powerful-jump-smash.html\">badminton jump smash<\/a>, you will <strong>be able to take the shuttlecock from a higher point<\/strong>.<\/p>\n<p>If you haven&#8217;t master this shot, I highly advise that you learn it because it will definitely help you produce high quality cross court smashes.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<p><a class=\"old-comments\" href=\"how-to-do-a-cross-court-overhead-badminton-smash-comment-form.html\">Click here to post comments<\/a><\/p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><a class=\"noplsin\" href=\"badminton-techniques-questions.html#INV\"><br \/>\nJoin in and write your own page! It&#8217;s easy to do. How? Simply click here to return to <b>Questions on Skills and Shots<\/b>.<\/a><\/p>\n<h3 class=\"fblikeste\">Like Masterbadminton.com?<\/h3>\n<div id=\"fb-root\"><script><![CDATA[(function(d,s,id){var js,fjs=d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0];if(d.getElementById(id)){return;}js=d.createElement(s);js.id=id;js.src=\"..\/connect.facebook.net\/en_US\/all.js#xfbml=1\";fjs.parentNode.insertBefore(js,fjs);}(document,'script','facebook-jssdk'));]]><\/script><\/p>\n<div align=\"left\"><\/div>\n<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<\/div>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>by tusha (paramaibo) Question: How can you take an overhead shuttle and smash it straight on the other side of the court? Answer: Hi Tusha, thanks for asking us a question. The rule of thumb to execute an overhead badminton smash is to get behind the shuttle first. Position yourself behind the shuttlecock while it [&hellip;]<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":1,"featured_media":0,"comment_status":"open","ping_s